  <p>Alex's net take-home pay is $54,908.50 per year, or approximately <strong>$4,575.71 per month</strong> before any additional voluntary deductions. Of the original $75,000 salary, 26.8% goes to taxes and pre-tax benefits, while the remaining 73.2% arrives in Alex's bank account. Critically, $8,000 of that "missing" money went directly into Alex's 401(k) and HSA — savings that still belong to Alex and will grow over time.</p>

